      "level": 1,
      "content": "Revise Inheritance"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We've already learned about inheritance in C++. Here's how we've been implementing inheritance so far,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "class Person {\n    // statements\n};\n\n\nclass Student: public Person {\n    // statements\n};"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the Student class is derived from the Person class. As a result,"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "Student can access all the non-private members of Person,",
        "Person cannot access the members of Student."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Notice the keyword public that is used during inheritance. This indicates that we are performing public inheritance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Based on the access modifiers (public, private, and protected), we can perform inheritance in 3 different modes:"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "Public Inheritance",
        "Protected Inheritance",
        "Private Inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's start with public inheritance in C++."
    },
